  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya - Expansion of drying facility for the production of Ketchup</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF Start-up Loan Sauce with a Cause B.V. (SWAC) is able to expand the existing drying facility with a local partner, Burton &amp; Bamber.  SWAC was founded with the aim of preventing waste and spoilage on small Kenyan farms. The goal is to dry harvested tomatoes and mangoes for the export market to Europe to make ketchup. Through a crowd funding campaign, SWAC has been able to set up a supply chain in the period 2018-2020 and to train and certify more than 100 farmers for export to the European market. SWAC supervises, trains and buys the harvest from the farmers, after which SWAC has the ketchup made by a third party in the Netherlands. Meanwhile, the ketchup can be found on the shelves of large supermarket chains and department stores. In order to grow further (scale-up phase), SWAC wants to invest in its own drying machine for tomatoes and mangoes. In addition, SWAC has a need for working capital due to the growth. The drying machine will be installed in Kenya at (Burton &amp; Bamber) to dry the tomatoes and mangoes for export as well as take care of the operation and maintenance of the machine. In an earlier phase, SWAC received a DGGF Technical Assistance subsidy aimed at further training of the farmers, development of the supply chain and partly pre-financing for the first larger import by cargo ship. The expected impact is local employment of approximately 75 FTE and knowledge exchange by training the staff. In direct impact, more than 1,100 Farmers are reached.</narrative>
  </description>
